# Mission control: supervise N agents from one grid, one row per task.
# Each row is a task, the agent working it, its live session status, a
# ground-truth check, and a verified cell: 'pending' until the agent
# claims done, then green only if the check agrees. The agent's reply is
# its claim (one word: done).
#
# F names the task a row waits for, and G says whether it's ready: when that
# task's check holds, not when its agent says done. Start an agent on a
# ready row.
#
# Start each agent with Run (headless) or Open Session (watchable);
# session status lands in <cell>_status. Adapt tasks and checks.
A1 = task
B1 = agent (its reply is its claim)
C1 = status
D1 = check
E1 = verified
F1 = after
G1 = ready
A2 = make the tests pass
B2 = @claude('do this task in the current repo: {A2}. reply with only the word done')
C2 = = {B2_status}
D2 = $ cargo test 2>&1 | grep -c 'test result: ok' # watch: src/**
E2 = = if({B2} == 'done', {D2} > 0, 'pending')
G2 = = if({F2} == '', 'ready', if(lookup({F2}, {$A$2:$A$20}, {$E$2:$E$20}) == 'true', 'ready', 'waiting'))
A3 = write release notes for the next version
B3 = @claude('do this task in the current repo: {A3}. create RELEASE_NOTES.md, then reply with only the word done')
C3 = = {B3_status}
D3 = $ test -s RELEASE_NOTES.md && echo 1 || echo 0 # watch: RELEASE_NOTES.md
E3 = = if({B3} == 'done', {D3} > 0, 'pending')
F3 = make the tests pass
G3 = = if({F3} == '', 'ready', if(lookup({F3}, {$A$2:$A$20}, {$E$2:$E$20}) == 'true', 'ready', 'waiting'))
human_hint =
